{"field":"sample-1","placeholder":true,"made_by":"pipeline/export/build_risks.py --kind heatclock (rules.yaml heat_clock)","labels":{"heatclock_today":{"sure":"estimate","status":"NOT YET VERIFIABLE","k":0,"n":0,"scale":"valley","rain_corrected":false,"sources":["power","ghcn","crop_calendar"],"scorecard":null},"heatclock_2040":{"sure":"estimate","status":"NOT YET VERIFIABLE","k":0,"n":0,"scale":"region","rain_corrected":false,"sources":["nexgddp","crop_calendar"],"scorecard":null}},"why":{"en":["Wheat: FAO-66 (FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 66, Crop yield response to water, 2012, p.98) says temperatures above 34 °C are possible during grain filling and can shrink the grain. It describes what is possible, not a tested limit, and does not say which temperature of the day: we count days whose highest temperature is above 34 °C.","Grain-filling weeks: the last growth stage of FAO-56, the 35 days before harvest. FAO-66 gives no grain-filling length (its India row: flowering 70-103 days and maturity 85-145 days after sowing), so our weeks may miss the first days of grain filling.","Potato: FAO-66 (p.187) puts cold stress at 1 °C and less and heat stress at 35 °C or more, with no crop stage, so we count the whole season: nights whose lowest temperature is 1 °C or less, and days whose highest is 35 °C or more. Varieties differ, and the damage depends on how strong and how long.","Wheat, from FAO's wheat book (Acevedo, Silva and Silva, 'Wheat growth and physiology', in Bread Wheat: Improvement and Production, FAO, 2002): 'Temperatures above 30°C during floret formation cause complete sterility', and frost harms 'between flag leaf emergence and ten days after anthesis' at 'minimum screen temperatures below 0°C'. Both checks are estimates.","Floret weeks: the book does not say when floret formation ends, so we count its whole stage, from floral initiation (day 20) to anthesis, when the wheat flowers (day 100), from its Table 3.1: sown 15 Oct: 4 Nov to 23 Jan; sown 15 Nov: 5 Dec to 23 Feb. It does not say which temperature of the day: we count days whose highest temperature is above 30 °C.","Frost weeks: Table 3.1 has no day for flag leaf emergence, so we start at heading (day 90), which follows it, and end ten days after anthesis (day 110): sown 15 Oct: 13 Jan to 2 Feb; sown 15 Nov: 13 Feb to 5 Mar. So our weeks may start a little late. We count nights whose lowest temperature is below 0 °C. Two checks point opposite ways: our nights count too many cold nights against Kathmandu Airport, but DHM's Bhaktapur normals put winter nights (November to April) 1.0-1.5 °C colder than ours. So the true number of frost nights may be lower or higher.","Table 3.1 counts days from emergence; we count from the sowing day (emergence comes about 4 days after sowing in FAO-66's India row), so our weeks may sit a few days early. Its spring wheat takes 140 days, as ours does. The dates are the same every year (a 365-day year).","Today: our weather 2002-2025 from NASA POWER (cells of about 55 km), corrected to Kathmandu Airport's thermometer. Our night temperatures count too many cold nights: in a check on years held back, they gave 15 nights below 2 °C where the station recorded 9. So the true number of cold nights is likely lower.","Around 2040: 23 climate models (NEX-GDDP-CMIP6, one cell of about 25 km), 2026-2040, on two paths: SSP2-4.5 (the world warms less) and SSP5-8.5 (the world warms more). The models are not corrected to our station, so each model's 2026-2040 is compared with its own 1995-2014. We show the middle model, and the lowest and highest.","Left out: the '8-35 °C' pollen figure at wheat flowering. It is from FAO-66's rice chapter, not wheat. Rice and lentil are left out too: we found no checked limit for them.","These are counts of past years and computer guesses, not a forecast.","The climate models' cell is the demo field's: both fields lie in the same 0.25 degree cell."],"ne":["गहुँ: FAO-66 (FAO सिँचाइ तथा निकास पत्र ६६, बालीको पानीप्रतिको उब्जनी, २०१२, पृष्ठ ९८) भन्छ, दाना भरिने बेला ३४ डिग्रीभन्दा बढी तापक्रम हुन सक्छ र दाना सानो पार्न सक्छ। यो हुन सक्ने कुरा हो, जाँचिएको सीमा होइन, र दिनको कुन तापक्रम भनेर लेखिएको छैन: हामी दिनको सबैभन्दा बढी तापक्रम ३४ डिग्रीभन्दा माथि भएका दिन गन्छौं।","दाना भरिने हप्ता: FAO-56 को अन्तिम चरण, काट्नुअघिका ३५ दिन। FAO-66 ले दाना भरिने अवधि दिँदैन (भारतको पङ्क्ति: रोपेको ७०–१०३ दिनमा फूल, ८५–१४५ दिनमा पाक्ने), त्यसैले हाम्रा हप्ताले दाना भरिने सुरुका केही दिन छुटाउन सक्छन्।","आलु: FAO-66 (पृष्ठ १८७) अनुसार १ डिग्री वा कम चिसो र ३५ डिग्री वा बढी गर्मी हानिकारक हो, बालीको चरण नभनी; त्यसैले हामी पूरै सिजन गन्छौं: सबैभन्दा कम तापक्रम १ डिग्री वा कम भएका रात, र सबैभन्दा बढी ३५ डिग्री वा बढी भएका दिन। जातअनुसार फरक पर्छ, र हानि कति कडा र कति लामो भन्नेमा भर पर्छ।","गहुँ, FAO को गहुँ पुस्तकबाट (Acevedo, Silva र Silva, 'Wheat growth and physiology', Bread Wheat: Improvement and Production, FAO, २००२): फूलका कोपिला बन्दा ३० डिग्रीभन्दा बढी तापक्रमले गहुँ पूरै बाँझो हुन्छ, र झण्डा-पात निस्केदेखि फुलेको दस दिनपछिसम्म ० डिग्रीभन्दा कमको तुषारोले हानि गर्छ। दुवै जाँच अनुमान हुन्।","फूलका कोपिला बन्ने हप्ता: पुस्तकले यो कहिले सकिन्छ भन्दैन, त्यसैले हामी पूरै चरण गन्छौं, फूल बन्न थाल्ने (दिन २०) देखि गहुँ फुल्ने (दिन १००) सम्म, यसको तालिका ३.१ अनुसार: अक्टोबर १५ मा रोपेको: नोभेम्बर ४ देखि जनवरी २३ सम्म; नोभेम्बर १५ मा रोपेको: डिसेम्बर ५ देखि फेब्रुअरी २३ सम्म। दिनको कुन तापक्रम भनेर लेखिएको छैन: हामी दिनको सबैभन्दा बढी तापक्रम ३० डिग्रीभन्दा माथि भएका दिन गन्छौं।","तुषारोका हप्ता: तालिका ३.१ मा झण्डा-पात निस्कने दिन छैन, त्यसैले हामी बाला निस्कने दिन (दिन ९०) बाट सुरु गर्छौं, जुन त्यसपछि आउँछ, र फुलेको दस दिनपछि (दिन ११०) सकाउँछौं: अक्टोबर १५ मा रोपेको: जनवरी १३ देखि फेब्रुअरी २ सम्म; नोभेम्बर १५ मा रोपेको: फेब्रुअरी १३ देखि मार्च ५ सम्म। त्यसैले हाम्रा हप्ता अलि ढिलो सुरु हुन सक्छन्। हामी सबैभन्दा कम तापक्रम ० डिग्रीभन्दा कम भएका रात गन्छौं। दुई जाँच उल्टो दिशा देखाउँछन्: हाम्रा रातले काठमाडौं विमानस्थलको तुलनामा चिसो रात धेरै गन्छन्, तर DHM को भक्तपुरको औसतमा जाडोका रात (नोभेम्बरदेखि अप्रिल) हाम्रोभन्दा १.०–१.५ डिग्री चिसा छन्। त्यसैले साँचो तुषारो रात कम वा बढी हुन सक्छन्।","तालिका ३.१ ले उम्रेको दिनदेखि गन्छ; हामी रोपेको दिनदेखि गन्छौं (FAO-66 को भारतको पङ्क्तिअनुसार रोपेको करिब ४ दिनमा उम्रन्छ), त्यसैले हाम्रा हप्ता केही दिन चाँडो पर्न सक्छन्। यसको वसन्ते गहुँ १४० दिनको हो, हाम्रो पनि त्यति नै। मिति हरेक वर्ष उस्तै हुन्छन् (३६५ दिनको वर्ष)।","आज: हाम्रो २००२–२०२५ को मौसम, NASA POWER बाट (करिब ५५ किलोमिटरका कोठा), काठमाडौं विमानस्थलको थर्मामिटरसँग मिलाइएको। हाम्रा रातका तापक्रमले चिसो रात धेरै गन्छन्: अलग राखिएका वर्षको जाँचमा २ डिग्रीभन्दा कमका १५ रात देखाए, केन्द्रले ९ रात मात्र नापेको थियो। त्यसैले साँचो चिसो रात कम हुन सक्छन्।","सन् २०४० तिर: २३ वटा जलवायु मोडेल (NEX-GDDP-CMIP6, करिब २५ किलोमिटरको एउटा कोठा), २०२६–२०४०, दुई बाटोमा: SSP2-4.5 (संसार कम तातिए) र SSP5-8.5 (संसार बढी तातिए)। मोडेलहरू हाम्रो केन्द्रसँग मिलाइएका छैनन्, त्यसैले हरेक मोडेलको २०२६–२०४० लाई उसैको आफ्नै १९९५–२०१४ सँग दाँजिएको छ। बीचको मोडेल, र सबैभन्दा कम र बढी देखाइएको छ।","छाडिएको: गहुँ फुल्ने बेलाको '८–३५ डिग्री' परागको अङ्क। यो FAO-66 को धानको अध्यायबाट हो, गहुँको होइन। धान र मसुर पनि छाडिएका छन्: तिनका लागि जाँचिएको सीमा भेटिएन।","यी विगतका वर्षको गन्ती र कम्प्युटरका अनुमान हुन्, पूर्वानुमान होइन।","जलवायु मोडेलको कोठा demo खेतकै हो: दुवै खेत एउटै ०.२५ डिग्रीको कोठामा पर्छन्।"],"ne_review":"needs native-speaker review","drafted_by":"SI (Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code), 2026-11-14"},"sources":[{"name":"NASA POWER","product":"Daily API v2.10.3 (MERRA-2 weather, CERES sunshine); temperatures corrected to Kathmandu Airport","resolution":"0.5 x 0.625 deg (about 55 km)","years":"2001-2025","type":"model"},{"name":"Kathmandu Airport station","product":"NOAA GHCN-Daily NP000444540 (temperature correction, checks)","resolution":"one point, 11 km west","years":"2001-2025","type":"station"},{"name":"NEX-GDDP-CMIP6","product":"daily, bias-corrected and downscaled (BCSD), v2.0","resolution":"0.25 deg","years":"1995-2014 and 2026-2040","type":"model"},{"name":"FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 66, Crop yield response to water","product":"wheat p.98 (above 34 C during grain filling), Table 1 p.95; potato p.187 (cold 1 C and less, heat 35 C or higher)","resolution":"a published text","years":"2012","type":"document"},{"name":"FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 56 (Allen et al. 1998)","product":"crop growth stages, chapter 6; stage lengths of our crop table from its Table 11, scaled to the local season","resolution":"a method","years":"1998","type":"document"},{"name":"Acevedo, Silva and Silva, 'Wheat growth and physiology', in Bread Wheat: Improvement and Production (FAO Plant Production and Protection Series No. 30)","product":"above 30 C during floret formation causes complete sterility; frost below 0 C (minimum screen temperature) from flag leaf emergence to ten days after anthesis; Table 3.1, days from emergence (spring wheat)","resolution":"a published text","years":"2002","type":"document"}],"years":[2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"year_count":24,"left_out":["rice","lentil","wheat pollen at flowering (8-35 C, a rice figure)"],"checks":[{"id":"potato_1030_cold","crop":"potato","sow":"10-30","end":"02-21","kind":"cold","stage":"season","window":{"from":"10-30","to":"02-21","days":115},"temperature":"daily minimum","column":"tmin_frost_c","rule":{"at_or_below_c":1},"plans":["current","rice_potato"],"today":{"years":[{"year":2002,"days":0},{"year":2003,"days":5},{"year":2004,"days":4},{"year":2005,"days":5},{"year":2006,"days":0},{"year":2007,"days":0},{"year":2008,"days":6},{"year":2009,"days":0},{"year":2010,"days":4},{"year":2011,"days":6},{"year":2012,"days":2},{"year":2013,"days":15},{"year":2014,"days":1},{"year":2015,"days":3},{"year":2016,"days":2},{"year":2017,"days":0},{"year":2018,"days":0},{"year":2019,"days":5},{"year":2020,"days":7},{"year":2021,"days":0},{"year":2022,"days":4},{"year":2023,"days":1},{"year":2024,"days":1}